---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { BUSINESS } from "../data/business.ts";

// Required before launch. The consent checkbox on /book/ links here.
const updated = "8 September 2026";
---

<Base
  title="Privacy notice — Quinton Carpets, Birmingham"
  description="What Quinton Carpets does with the name, address, phone number and email you give us when you book a free measure: why we hold it, how long for, and how to ask us to delete it."
>
  <div class="section plain">
    <div class="wrap" style="max-width:720px">
      <p class="eyebrow">Privacy</p>
      <h1 style="font-size:clamp(1.9rem,1.25rem + 2.5vw,3rem); margin-bottom:14px">
        What we do with your details.
      </h1>
      <p class="lede" style="margin-bottom:14px">
        Short version: we take your name, address, phone number and email so a fitter can turn
        up at the right house at the right time. We don't sell it, we don't share it, and you
        can have it deleted whenever you like.
      </p>
      <p class="hint" style="margin-bottom:34px">Last updated {updated}.</p>

      <div class="stack" style="gap:28px">
        <section>
          <h2 style="font-size:clamp(1.15rem,1rem + .6vw,1.5rem); margin-bottom:8px">Who we are</h2>
          <p style="color:var(--ink-2)">
            Quinton Carpets, {BUSINESS.street}, {BUSINESS.city}, {BUSINESS.postcode}. We are
            the data controller for everything described here. Phone
            <a href={BUSINESS.phoneHref}>&nbsp;{BUSINESS.phone}</a>, email
            <a href={`mailto:${BUSINESS.email}`}>&nbsp;{BUSINESS.email}</a>.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 style="font-size:clamp(1.15rem,1rem + .6vw,1.5rem); margin-bottom:8px">What we collect</h2>
          <p style="color:var(--ink-2); margin-bottom:10px">
            When you book a free measure on this website, we collect:
          </p>
          <ul style="color:var(--ink-2); padding-left:20px; display:grid; gap:6px">
            <li>your name;</li>
            <li>the address and postcode we're measuring;</li>
            <li>your phone number and email address;</li>
            <li>the day and time window you picked;</li>
            <li>anything you type in the notes box;</li>
            <li>an estimate code or a friend's referral code, if you have one.</li>
          </ul>
          <p style="color:var(--ink-2); margin-top:12px">
            We do not take payment on this website at any point, so we never collect card or
            bank details here. Money is taken in the shop.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 style="font-size:clamp(1.15rem,1rem + .6vw,1.5rem); margin-bottom:8px">Why we hold it</h2>
          <p style="color:var(--ink-2)">
            To ring you back and confirm the appointment, to send a fitter to the right
            address, and to keep a record of the job. If you used a friend's referral code we
            also record that, so the right discount reaches the right person.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 style="font-size:clamp(1.15rem,1rem + .6vw,1.5rem); margin-bottom:8px">Our lawful basis</h2>
          <p style="color:var(--ink-2)">
            Booking a measure and carrying out the work is <b>performance of a contract</b>, or
            the steps you asked us to take before one. Contacting you by phone or text about
            that booking rests on the <b>consent</b> you give with the tick box on the booking
            form; you can withdraw it any time by telling us, and it won't affect anything we
            did beforehand. Keeping invoices for the taxman is a <b>legal obligation</b>.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 style="font-size:clamp(1.15rem,1rem + .6vw,1.5rem); margin-bottom:8px">Who sees it</h2>
          <p style="color:var(--ink-2)">
            The people in the shop and the fitters doing your job. The website runs on
            Cloudflare, who host the site and the booking database, and confirmation emails go
            out through our email provider. Those companies process the data on our
            instructions and for nothing else. We do not sell your details or pass them to
            anyone for marketing.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 style="font-size:clamp(1.15rem,1rem + .6vw,1.5rem); margin-bottom:8px">How long we keep it</h2>
          <p style="color:var(--ink-2)">
            A booking that doesn't turn into a job: <b>12 months</b>, then deleted. A completed
            job: <b>6 years</b> from the end of the tax year, because that's how long we have
            to keep the paperwork. Referral codes are kept while they can still be used.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 style="font-size:clamp(1.15rem,1rem + .6vw,1.5rem); margin-bottom:8px">Your rights</h2>
          <p style="color:var(--ink-2); margin-bottom:10px">
            You can ask us for a copy of what we hold, ask us to correct it, ask us to delete
            it, or object to us using it. Ring the shop or email us and we'll sort it — there's
            nothing to fill in and no charge. We'll answer within one month.
          </p>
          <p style="color:var(--ink-2)">
            To ask for deletion, email
            <a href={`mailto:${BUSINESS.email}?subject=Please%20delete%20my%20details`}>&nbsp;{BUSINESS.email}</a>
            with your booking reference, or ring
            <a href={BUSINESS.phoneHref}>&nbsp;{BUSINESS.phone}</a>. We'll delete everything we
            aren't legally required to keep.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 style="font-size:clamp(1.15rem,1rem + .6vw,1.5rem); margin-bottom:8px">Cookies</h2>
          <p style="color:var(--ink-2)">
            This site sets no tracking cookies and carries no advertising. The estimator keeps
            your estimate code in your own browser so the booking form can fill it in for you;
            that never leaves your device and is gone when you close the tab.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 style="font-size:clamp(1.15rem,1rem + .6vw,1.5rem); margin-bottom:8px">Complaints</h2>
          <p style="color:var(--ink-2)">
            Tell us first and we'll try to put it right. If you're still not happy you can
            complain to the Information Commissioner's Office at
            <a href="https://ico.org.uk/make-a-complaint/" rel="noopener">&nbsp;ico.org.uk</a>.
          </p>
        </section>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
